} :question/id #uuid "812ad39a-35a8-5d8f-9bb3-4d47c582659b" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$. Find the missing entries of $C^3$.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$C^3=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$-1$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>$1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$2$</td><td>$1$</td><td>{{field-5}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "First compute $C^2$ by multiplying rows of $C$ by columns of $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C^2 &= C\\cdot C \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}1-1+0 & -1+0+0 & 0-1+0 \\\\ 1+0+0 & -1+0+1 & 0+0+1 \\\\ 0+1+0 & 0+0+1 & 0+1+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow use $C^3=C^2\\cdot C$:\n\n$$\nC^3=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe five missing entries are obtained from these row-by-column products:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(C^3)_{11} &= 0\\cdot1+(-1)\\cdot1+(-1)\\cdot0=-1 \\\\ (C^3)_{13} &= 0\\cdot0+(-1)\\cdot1+(-1)\\cdot1=-2 \\\\ (C^3)_{21} &= 1\\cdot1+0\\cdot1+1\\cdot0=1 \\\\ (C^3)_{22} &= 1\\cdot(-1)+0\\cdot0+1\\cdot1=0 \\\\ (C^3)_{33} &= 1\\cdot0+1\\cdot1+2\\cdot1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719720 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e457e7b-ecc2-5fe6-804c-05ab81de7287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218671